  "links": [],
  "text": [
    "Chains",
    "A chained seat passes fire and thunder damage along to every other chained seat.",
    "Chaining and Unchaining",
    "Play Chains on 1 or 2 seats at any distance, yourself included. Each unchained target becomes chained, and each chained target becomes unchained. You may also recast it: discard it and draw 1 card.",
    "The Chain Wave",
    "Only fire and thunder damage travels. Plain damage never does. When a chained seat takes fire or thunder damage, it is unchained, and every other chained seat then takes the same damage, one at a time, in turn order starting after the damaged seat. A seat hit this way does not start a wave of its own.",
    "Example: 1 Fire Damage on Seat 2",
    "Seats 2, 3 and 5 are chained. Seat 1 uses Fire Attack and Seat 2 takes 1 fire damage.→Seat 2Wu4 HPSeat 3Shu4 HPSeat 5Qun4 HP",
    "Seats 2, 3 and 5 are chained. Seat 1 uses Fire Attack and Seat 2 takes 1 fire damage.",
    "Seat 2 loses 1 HP and is unchained.Seat 2Wu3 HPSeat 3Shu4 HPSeat 5Qun4 HP",
    "Seat 2 loses 1 HP and is unchained.",
    "The other chained seats are hit one at a time in turn order after Seat 2: Seat 3, then Seat 5. Each takes the original 1 damage, changed only by its own effects, and is unchained. If a hit starts a dying round, that round finishes before the next seat is hit.Seat 2Wu3 HPSeat 3Shu3 HPSeat 5Qun3 HP",
    "The other chained seats are hit one at a time in turn order after Seat 2: Seat 3, then Seat 5. Each takes the original 1 damage, changed only by its own effects, and is unchained. If a hit starts a dying round, that round finishes before the next seat is hit.",
