{
  "links": [],
  "text": [
    "Response Windows",
    "Some cards give another seat a chance to answer before anything happens. This page follows two of them from start to finish.",
    "Slash and Dodge",
    "Seat 1 plays Slash on Seat 3, who is in range.Seat 1Wei→Seat 3Shu",
    "Seat 1 plays Slash on Seat 3, who is in range.",
    "A response window opens for Seat 3. The seat may play a Dodge or pass.Plays DodgeThe Slash has no effect. Nothing is lost.PassesSeat 3 takes 1 damage and drops to 3 HP.",
    "A response window opens for Seat 3. The seat may play a Dodge or pass.",
    "Wuxie on a Tool",
    "Before a Tool takes effect, the game checks for Wuxie. It asks the living seats in seat order, starting from the seat that used the Tool, and only those that hold a Wuxie at that moment. Passing asks the next holder. Passes are not announced, so nobody learns who held one.",
    "Example: Break With a Wuxie Chain",
    "Seat 1 plays Break on Seat 4. The Tool is about to take effect.Waiting for a Wuxie check",
    "Seat 1 plays Break on Seat 4. The Tool is about to take effect.",
    "Seat 2 holds a Wuxie and plays it. Break is cancelled, unless someone counters.Break cancelled",
    "Seat 2 holds a Wuxie and plays it. Break is cancelled, unless someone counters.",
    "The check restarts from the seat after Seat 2, and a seat is never asked about its own card. Seat 3 plays a Wuxie on that Wuxie.First Wuxie cancelled",
    "The check restarts from the seat after Seat 2, and a seat is never asked about its own card. Seat 3 plays a Wuxie on that Wuxie.",
    "Nobody answers again, so Break goes ahead. Any length of chain works the same way: the last Wuxie decides.Break takes effect",
    "Nobody answers again, so Break goes ahead. Any length of chain works the same way: the last Wuxie decides.",
    "Wuxie on a Tool That Hits Many Seats",
    "A Tool such as Barbarians runs its own Wuxie check for each target in turn. A Wuxie spares only the target it was played for.",
